Half-precision (FEAT_FP16) emitters on the arm64 backend

Why: the A64 frontend translates the scalar FABS, FNEG, FMADD, FMSUB, FRINT*, FRECPE, FRECPX,
FRECPS, FRSQRTE and FRSQRTS on H registers and the vector FNEG, FCMEQ, FMLA, FRECPE, FRECPS,
FRSQRTE and FRSQRTS on .8H/.4H, and the arm64 backend left their opcodes unimplemented (an abort
when a block uses them). Each is the host's own instruction (every Apple silicon host has
FEAT_FP16); the vector ones through the helpers the single-precision forms use, which already
take 16-bit lanes, and the scalar forms oaknut has no mnemonic for (FABS, FNEG, FMADD, FMSUB,
FRINT*) as their A64 encodings. FPHalfToFixed* and FPVectorTo*Fixed16 stay unimplemented: the
frontend at this commit never emits them (it rejects or does not decode those encodings).
emulator/src/cpu.rs's patched_emitters_agree_with_the_host runs each through the JIT and on
the host and compares.

Upstream: azahar-emu/dynarmic a46601580d55 (its master on 2026-11-12) lacks these; they are
not sent upstream.

